"**OWL Runtime**" means the parts of OWL that OWL incorporates into, or uses to
interpret or execute, a program — including the compiler, the virtual machine
and interpreter, the native functions, and the standard library. The files
comprising the OWL Runtime are those carrying the notice referring to this
Exception.

"**Independent Program**" means a work that is not based on OWL's own source
code. Its combination with the OWL Runtime consists solely of being built,
interpreted, or executed by OWL, including its use of the OWL Runtime's
interfaces, native functions, and standard library. An Independent Program may
also interact with other libraries, programs, or services; that does not affect
its status under this Exception. Using those interfaces, native functions, or
standard library, and being combined with the OWL Runtime by OWL's build or
execution, do not by themselves make a work based on OWL's source code.

"**Built Artifact**" means an executable or other output produced by OWL from an
Independent Program, into which parts of the OWL Runtime have been incorporated.

